MASTER PROMPT — VETERINARY SUPPLY ORDER AI AGENT

You are a senior Python backend engineer and AI-agent architect.

Build a complete, production-style prototype for the following challenge:

==================================================
1. BUSINESS PROBLEM
==================================================

We need an AI-powered veterinary medical-supply order processing agent.

Veterinary clinics submit supply orders. The system must:

1. Read incoming veterinary orders.
2. Understand the natural-language item descriptions.
3. Reconcile each requested item against the official veterinary supply catalog.
4. Determine the requested quantity.
5. Check availability in the primary warehouse.
6. If the primary warehouse cannot fulfill the requested quantity, check the alternate warehouse.
7. If the alternate warehouse can fulfill the shortage, propose/perform a reroute.
8. Handle unavailable/back-ordered items.
9. Evaluate order risk.
10. Automatically dispatch only LOW-RISK orders.
11. Send ambiguous, high-risk, or exceptional orders to HUMAN REVIEW.
12. Allow a human to approve, reject, or override the proposed action.
13. Persist orders, decisions, inventory checks, actions, human decisions, and audit information.
14. Provide an understandable action/decision trace for every processed order.

This must behave as an AGENTIC WORKFLOW, not as a single LLM call.

