11. RISK ENGINE
==================================================

Implement a deterministic risk engine.

Do NOT let the LLM freely decide whether an order is safe to dispatch.

The risk engine should consider factors such as:

- ambiguous catalog match
- missing SKU
- low confidence match
- insufficient primary inventory
- alternate warehouse involvement
- back-order
- invalid inventory data
- unusual/invalid quantities
- missing required order information
- tool/action errors

Return:

{
    "risk_level": "LOW | MEDIUM | HIGH",
    "reasons": [...]
}

Only LOW-risk orders may be automatically dispatched.

MEDIUM/HIGH-risk orders must enter human review unless an explicit documented rule says otherwise.

Keep risk rules transparent and configurable.

